Return a null declaration from Linkage::specializeGeneric when the generic application fails to check.

Linkage::specializeGeneric (source/slang/slang-session.cpp), behind spReflection_specializeGeneric
and ProgramLayout::specializeGeneric, checks the application of the generic to the caller's
arguments and takes the declaration out of the result unconditionally:

    auto specializedDeclRef =
        as<DeclRefExpr>(visitor.checkGenericAppWithCheckedArgs(genericAppExpr))->declRef;   // 808-809

When the arguments do not match the generic's parameters (an integer where a type parameter
belongs, or two type arguments for one parameter), checkGenericAppWithCheckedArgs diagnoses it
("expected a type", "too many arguments") and returns an error expression: the GenericAppExpr
itself, from CreateErrorExpr in CompleteOverloadCandidate (source/slang/slang-check-overload.cpp,
the error label). as<DeclRefExpr> of that is null, and the member access dereferences it. The
behaviour is undefined, and the release shows it: an access violation on Windows x64 and on Linux
x86-64 and aarch64, and on macOS arm64 a non-null generic returned beside the diagnostic.

This checks the cast and returns a null DeclRef, which spReflection_specializeGeneric returns as
null alongside the diagnostics the check already produced. A matching argument list takes the
same path as before. A regression test is added as
tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-specialize-generic-mismatch.cpp.

Measured on v2026.21 with struct MgWrapper<T : IMgMaterial>: before, both mismatches access-violate
(win-x64, 0xC0000005); after, null with "expected a type" and with "too many arguments"
respectively (win-x64, linux-x64).
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-session.cpp b/source/slang/slang-session.cpp
index 15e3a1f51..a7931f933 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-session.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-session.cpp
@@ -805,10 +805,16 @@ DeclRef<Decl> Linkage::specializeGeneric(
     genericAppExpr->functionExpr = declRefExpr;
     genericAppExpr->arguments = argExprs;
 
-    auto specializedDeclRef =
-        as<DeclRefExpr>(visitor.checkGenericAppWithCheckedArgs(genericAppExpr))->declRef;
+    // Checking the application diagnoses an argument list that does not match the generic's
+    // parameters, and the result is then an error expression rather than a reference to the
+    // specialized declaration.
+    //
+    auto specializedDeclRefExpr =
+        as<DeclRefExpr>(visitor.checkGenericAppWithCheckedArgs(genericAppExpr));
+    if (!specializedDeclRefExpr)
+        return DeclRef<Decl>();
 
-    return specializedDeclRef;
+    return specializedDeclRefExpr->declRef;
 }
 
 SLANG_NO_THROW slang::TypeLayoutReflection* SLANG_MCALL Linkage::getTypeLayout(
